    "reader_source_note": "Latin printed witness. Reading order follows the inspected body columns on scan leaves 494–497 (printed pages 456–459). The marginal summaries and all historical notes remain included as separate blocks. Eight uncertain interline OCR recognitions are retained separately from continuous prose. The historical apparatus records tentative lexical conjectures, alternative readings and an editorially added word; its wording remains literal, and no further words are supplied or adopted. The printed sections 1–4 and full and short dating survive. Page reordering changes serialization and whitespace between intact XML WORDs. OCR characters have not been collated throughout against the images, and historical attribution and dating have not been authenticated.",
    "registration_instruction": "Create a separately identified new whole-volume ordered controller from this recipe and bind this reviewed act to its exact disjoint LF ranges with a new segment/witness identity. Preserve all withdrawn predecessor records and bytes. Do not replace or reactivate the old single-page controller.",
    "remaining_geometry_blockers_for_this_act": [],
    "remaining_source_pages_read_only_as_OCR": [],
    "review_note": "The independent CCCXXIV heading is source WORD 259550 (raw LF 65373), followed by synopsis WORDs 259551–259578 and the actual Paulus self-protocol/addressee WORDs 259579–259600 (raw LF 65383–65387). The full opening and section 1 run from leaf 494 into the complete leaf 495 left column; its ending WORDs 259924–259930 precede the top-right continuation WORDs 259718–259723, which then precede WORDs 259973 onward. Section 2 begins at WORD 260098 and continues without marginal injections into leaf 496 left; section 3 begins at WORD 260491 in leaf 496 right, and section 4 at WORD 260661 continues into leaf 497 left. Full and short dating WORDs 260789–260814 (raw LF 65638–65643) close before independent CCCXXV WORD 260815. All own historical notes are retained: the source reference at raw LF 65408; three left-column notes at 65458–65465; the right-column lexical variant at 65520; the possible-preposition note at 65569–65570; and the editorial word-addition note at 65620. The tentative notes do not announce an omitted substantive opening, body or annex. Each source note/marker relationship and the complete substantive body were read, not only the three formerly known repair loci. Separable own marginal WORDs from leaves 494, 495 and 496 are now outside continuous body streams. Eight interline recognition WORDs on 495 are preserved in a distinct uncertain block. The vertical-rule recognitions WORDs 259717 and 260750 remain in the whole container, outside the selected act. No indivisible owned body/caption WORD fusion was found; all eight multi-token owned XML WORDs contain body tokens from their single printed line and remain unpartitioned. No source characters are edited, reconstructed or translated. This admits a complete printed OCR witness, not a critically authenticated historical act or complete autograph.",
